# The drives through their drivers (roadmap os-server.md P14): init starts
# tests/posix/drives.c (TEST_POSIX_DRIVES). On each of A to D a file is
# written, fsync'd and read back, one of three sectors too; the boot
# diskette's KERNEL.BIN is read whole; no drive E, and a buffer past the
# data's end, are refused. After the run fsck.fat finds every volume
# sound, and mtools reads each file as the program left it. On MAME, whose
# diskettes take the AT's time, a sector a turn, KERNEL.BIN takes half a
# minute: the run ends once the lines are all there. DOSBox-X has no drive
# C, and no interrupt from its diskette controller (docs/emulators.md).
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_DRIVES
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: prefix
timeout: 300
emulators: bochs mame
fsck: A
fsck: B
fsck: C
fsck: D
file: A /DRIVES.TXT rx286 wrote this to A\n
file: B /DRIVES.TXT rx286 wrote this to B\n
file: C /DRIVES.TXT rx286 wrote this to C\n
file: D /DRIVES.TXT rx286 wrote this to D\n
---
rx286, test build
drives: A: KERNEL.BIN read: {image_size} bytes
drives: A: a file written: errno 0, read back: the same
drives: A: 1500 bytes written: errno 0, read back: the same
drives: B: a file written: errno 0, read back: the same
drives: B: 1500 bytes written: errno 0, read back: the same
drives: C: a file written: errno 0, read back: the same
drives: C: 1500 bytes written: errno 0, read back: the same
drives: D: a file written: errno 0, read back: the same
drives: D: 1500 bytes written: errno 0, read back: the same
drives: no drive E (-1, ENOENT 2): -1, errno 2
drives: a read past the data's end (-1, EFAULT 14): -1, errno 14
drives: done
